<https://decision-cli.dev/ns/ex/EX-CLI-INSPECT> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns#basedOnApprovedResult> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/result/VGR-024> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/graph/catalog> .
<https://decision-cli.dev/ns/ex/EX-CLI-INSPECT> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns#rationale> "Pattern for verifying that a CLI surface exposes the expected subcommand or flag. Each step runs `dec <subcmd> --help` and asserts exit 0. Cheap, fast, and the right tool when the TC's claim is about command availability rather than runtime behaviour. Don't use for behavioural verification — for that, run the subcommand and assert observable effects." <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/graph/catalog> .
<https://decision-cli.dev/ns/ex/EX-CLI-INSPECT> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns#patternName> "cli-help-inspection" <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/graph/catalog> .
<https://decision-cli.dev/ns/ex/EX-CLI-INSPECT> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns#appliesToSafetyClass> "isolated" <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/graph/catalog> .
<https://decision-cli.dev/ns/ex/EX-CLI-INSPECT> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns#exemplarOf> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/graph/VG-017> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/graph/catalog> .
<https://decision-cli.dev/ns/ex/EX-CLI-INSPECT> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns#ExemplarGraph> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/graph/catalog> .
